; CultivatedCropsPlot — one of 2 Cultivated field terrain variants. Composes a
; root-vegetable/mixed-plot look (tomato, pumpkin, and cabbage-style rows) as the second
; crop-type variant alongside CultivatedWheatRow, per the task's "2-3 crop-type variants"
; guidance — reasonable variety without implying growth-stage simulation (v1 has no such
; mechanic; this is a single fixed visual stage, not an animated progression).
;
; Source: CropsPlot.glb, "Crops" by Quaternius, CC0 1.0 Universal, poly.pizza — see
; project/attribution/sources/quaternius_poly_pizza_nature.tres. This single mesh is
; ALREADY composed as 5 furrow rows (tomato, pumpkin, and 2 cabbage-style rows) with soil
; strips baked in — chosen over hand-placing individual crop props because it already
; reads as "a small farm plot," which is exactly the brief ("a few crop rows/furrows, not
; a single plant in the middle of a box").
;
; Raw measured AABB: footprint 1.789x1.556, height 0.323 tile-units — bigger than one
; 0.94-unit tile at native scale. Scaled to 0.48 (footprint ~0.86x0.75, height ~0.155),
; leaving a visible soil-slab margin on every edge so the tile-to-tile boundary stays
; readable. FLAG FOR HUMAN SIGN-OFF: this scale trades off row-count legibility (rows
; compress at this size) against tile-fit; a human may prefer either a further scale-down
; for more headroom or a slight crop/mask to the AABB instead.
;
; Slab matches CultivatedWheatRow's dirt-brown (Color(0.4, 0.28, 0.16, 1)) for tonal
; consistency across both Cultivated field variants — the crop mesh's own baked-in soil
; color is a similar tone, so the slab mostly shows as a narrow worked-soil margin.
;
; SLAB WIDENED 0.94 -> 1.0 (2026-08-16, human-reported cross-tile seam gap) — same fix,
; same reasoning as CommonTree1.tscn's header. X/Z only, Y (0.2) untouched. This slightly
; narrows the visible soil margin the header above describes, but the crop mesh itself is
; untouched (still scaled to 0.48, well inside the now-1.0 footprint).
